---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="NO BALL GAMES Collections | Originals, Wearables, Digital Collectibles & XRP KIDs"
  description="Collector-facing overview of NO BALL GAMES originals, painted clothing, digital collectibles and XRP KIDs canon with strict verify-before-interaction warnings."
  current="collections"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Collections</span>
    <h1>Collect the story in physical and digital form.</h1>
    <p>
      This page separates physical collecting from digital collecting so buyers, fans and researchers know what is available now, what is canon concept, and what still needs source verification.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Collector categories</h2>
      <p>Original art, painted clothing, digital collectibles and XRP KIDs concept lanes.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Original art</span>
        <h3>One-of-one painted works</h3>
        <p>Sign-flip canvases, portrait-led pieces, mixed-media experiments and raw studio output grounded in NO BALL GAMES and Grime Art identity.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Painted clothing</span>
        <h3>Wearable art pieces</h3>
        <p>Hand-painted jackets, denim and custom garments produced as collectible wearables rather than mass production merch.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Digital collectibles</span>
        <h3>Lore-led digital objects</h3>
        <p>Character drops, collector passes and story-linked releases that should stay tied to canon and clear source labels.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">XRP KIDs concept</span>
        <h3>100 / 89 / 11 internal canon</h3>
        <p>XRP KIDs appears here as an internal lore branch featuring Alpha Aaron, FRET, $PMSL and Block Buster OG until on-chain records are verified.</p>
        <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}xrp/`}>Open XRP collector context →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section split-grid">
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Physical collector lane</span>
      <h2>What physical collectors should expect.</h2>
      <ul class="list-clean">
        <li>Original artworks with medium, size and provenance notes.</li>
        <li>Painted clothing with garment base and finish details.</li>
        <li>Limited editions and commissions via direct enquiry.</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}contact/`}>Enquire about physical pieces →</a>
    </article>

    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Digital collector lane</span>
      <h2>What digital collectors should verify first.</h2>
      <ul class="list-clean">
        <li>Verify issuer before interacting with any token or collectible.</li>
        <li>Verify collection records and marketplace listings.</li>
        <li>Treat lore text as canon narrative, not automatic chain proof.</li>
        <li>Avoid acting on unverified supply, price or holder claims.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="coming-soon-tag">Verify issuer • Verify collection • Verify marketplace</div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-block">
    <div class="cta-block-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Collector support</span>
      <h2>Need clarity before you collect?</h2>
      <p>Use contact for originals, wearables, digital collectible context, lore questions and source/proof checks.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}contact/`}>Contact collector desk</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}research/`}>Read source archive</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
